※ There have to be as many names as the tuple has members: a member with no
※ name would be a value the program worked out and threw away without saying
※ so.

fn three() → 〈u8, u8, u8〉:
    〈1u8, 2u8, 3u8〉

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let a, b := three()
    a + b
